  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3201aeaf-2efa-4359-9909-37dee60888a0-image.png\" style=\"width: 80px; height: 176px;\" /></p><p>To balance gravitational force, electric force on the liquid drop should act in upward direction.</p><p>For translational equilibrium along vertical direction,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p>",
